From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 21:29:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8998-google-taimen: describe the
 fingerprint irq as a gpio

The fingerprint trustlet's capture protocol waits on the interrupt
line's level, and msm pinctrl's irqchip cannot report a line level, so
the fpc1020 driver reads it from a GPIO and derives the interrupt from
that. Describe tlmm 86 as irq-gpios instead of an interrupt.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts | 12 +++++-------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts
index 130da3c782cf..8540fe233c60 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts
@@ -342,10 +342,10 @@ touchscreen@49 {
  *
  * GPIOs and the supply are the vendor's own
  * (msm8998-taimen-fingerprint.dtsi): fpc,gpio_rst = tlmm 128,
- * fpc,gpio_irq = tlmm 86 (interrupts = <86 0x0>, i.e. no explicit
- * trigger type recorded -- fpc1020_platform_tee.c's probe() arms it
- * IRQF_TRIGGER_RISING regardless of the DT interrupt flags, and that
- * value is used here too). vcc_spi-supply and vdd_ana-supply are
+ * fpc,gpio_irq = tlmm 86. The interrupt is described as a GPIO rather
+ * than an interrupt because its level is what the trustlet's capture
+ * protocol waits on, and msm pinctrl cannot report a line level through
+ * the irqchip. vcc_spi-supply and vdd_ana-supply are
  * commented out in the vendor's own taimen node -- not invented here
  * either; vdd_io-supply = pm8998_s4 (mainline label vreg_s4a_1p8, the
  * same rail the codec and UFS already use) is the only supply this
@@ -355,9 +355,7 @@ &soc {
 	fingerprint@0 {
 		compatible = "fpc,fpc1020";
 
-		interrupt-parent = <&tlmm>;
-		interrupts = <86 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
-
+		irq-gpios = <&tlmm 86 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		reset-gpios = <&tlmm 128 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		vdd-io-supply = <&vreg_s4a_1p8>;
 
